nodecode-empiriolabs-media is a rewrite of EmpirioLabs-AI's EmpirioLabs-AI/hermes-empiriolabs:

  https://github.com/EmpirioLabs-AI/hermes-empiriolabs
  commit 20f049d5913ec850e98bef3d289f6cb43645869e
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 EmpirioLabs.ai LLC (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the `media` folder at that commit: a Hermes backend
that serves the standard image_generate, video_generate and text_to_speech
tools from EmpirioLabs AI's API. Its wire is carried over unchanged: POST
/v1/images/generations with num_images 1 and sync, POST /v1/videos/generations,
POST /v1/audio/speech, all against https://api.empiriolabs.ai/v1 (or
EMPIRIOLABS_BASE_URL) with the key as a bearer; the job envelope — a job id
with no output means poll GET /v1/jobs/{job_id} every 3 seconds for an image
and 5 for a video, up to the deadline, and a job still running when the wait
ends is reported by id and URL rather than as a failure; the output read from
data[].url or data[].b64_json; a signed URL downloaded without the key and
written into this home; the local source image read once, capped at 20 MB,
sniffed as PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF and inlined as a data:image URI; the
answer's fallbacks (base64 written whole, and the signed URL kept when the
copy fails); the release defaults flux-2-klein-4b, hunyuan-video-1-5 and
tts-2-flash; the semantic aspect table (square 1:1, landscape 16:9, portrait
9:16, the original's first choice with no catalog); the 300- and 900-second
waits; and the EMPIRIOLABS_API_KEY and EMPIRIOLABS_BASE_URL variables,
turned into the cell's section with EMPIRIOLABS_API_KEY read either way.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes backend interface itself
(agent.image_gen_provider, agent.video_gen_provider and agent.tts_provider
with register_image_gen_provider, register_video_gen_provider and
register_tts_provider), because Nodecode's core has no media-backend registry
a cell can add one to, so each endpoint is a tool of the cell's own
(empiriolabs_image, empiriolabs_video, empiriolabs_speech) with the same
verbs in Lisp, /empiriolabs-media and (help :empiriolabs-media) beside them;
the live catalog negotiation — GET /v1/models read to choose the default
model, to limit aspect_ratio, size, resolution and duration to the values a
model declares, to list its voices and to cap a speech request — because a
call here sends only what the caller names plus the section's defaults, and
(empiriolabs-media:models) still reads that catalog for whoever wants it; the
text-to-speech sentence split with its ID3-stripped MP3 pieces joined back
to back, because one request now carries the text and a text longer than the
model accepts is the API's own refusal; the model-picker rows, the paid
badge and the manifest's env-var prompts, which the cell's section carries;
and Python's urllib and threading, replaced by the image's own nlk:http.
Generated files land under this home's media/empiriolabs/ rather than in
Hermes's cache directory, and no telemetry was added or removed: the original
sends none.
